<div id="header">
<h1>Accessing the JRuby Instance</h1>
</div>
<div id="content">
<div class="paragraph">
<p>Sometimes you may need the Ruby runtime used inside AsciidoctorJ.
One reason is because you are using JRuby outside AsciidoctorJ and you want to reuse the same instance.
Another reason is that you need to instantiate by yourself an Asciidoctor Ruby object.</p>
</div>
<div class="paragraph">
<p>To get this instance you can use <code>org.asciidoctor.jruby.internal.JRubyRuntimeContext.get(Asciidoctor)</code> to get it from a given Asciidoctor instance.</p>
</div>
</div>
